$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Wang resin (50 mg, 0.93 mmol/g) was placed in a 3 mL-polypropylene
syringe fitted with a polyethylene filter disc. The resin was then washed
with DMF (3 x 1 min) and CH2Cl2 (3 x 1 min). Fmoc-Gly-OH (110 mg, 0.37
mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2-DMF (9:1) and DIPCDI (28.8 μL, 0.19 mmol)
was added. The mixture was then added to the resin and DMAP (4.5 mg, 0.04
mmol) in DMF (0.2 mL) was finally added and the mixture was reacted for
14 h at 25 °C. The Fmoc-Gly-O-Wang resin was subjected to the following
washings/treatments: filtration, CH2Cl2 (3 x 1 min), DMF (3 x 1 min),
piperidine-DMF (1:4) (1 x 1 min, 2 x 5 min). Next, Fmoc-D-Ser(Trt)-OH
(76.8 mg, 0.135 mmol) was introduced with HATU (51.3 mg, 0.135 mmol) as
coupling reagent in DMF in the presence of DIEA (45.9 μL, 0.27 mmol) to
the peptide resin. The mixture was stirred for 1 h and, after filtration,
Kaiser test indicated the completion of the coupling reaction. The
peptide resin was then washed with DMF (3 x 1 min), CH2Cl2 (3 x 1 min),
and treated with piperidine-DMF (1:4) (1 x 1 min, 2 x 5 min) to remove
the Fmoc group. In order to introduce the pNZ group, the resin was
treated with p-nitrobenzyl chloroformate (29.1 μL, 0.135 mmol) and DIEA
(229 μL, 1.35 mmol) in CH2Cl2 for 45 min. Removal of the trityl group was
accomplished by washings with TFA-TIS-CH2Cl2 (2:2.5:95.5) until a
colorless filtrate was obtained. The peptide-resin was then washed with
CH2Cl2 (3 x 1 min) and Alloc-NMe-Cys(Me)-OH (104.8 mg, 0.45 mmol) was
introduced by reaction with DIPCDI (69.7 μL, 0.45 mmol) and DMAP (5.5 mg,
0.045 mmol) in DMF-CH2Cl2 (1:9) for 14 h at 25 °C. To remove the Alloc
group, the peptide-resin was treated with Pd(PPh3)4 (5.2 mg, 4.5 μmol)
and PhSiH3 (55.4 mg, 0.45 mmol) dissolved in CH2Cl2 (4 x 15 min) under
Ar, and was then washed with CH2Cl2 (3 x 1 min). The process was repeated
three times and Boc-NMe-Cys(Acm)-OH (68.8 mg, 0.225 mmol) was introduced
with (85.6 mg, 0.225 mmol), HOAt (30.7 mg, 0.225 mmol), and DIEA (45.9
μL, 0.27 mmol) as coupling system. The coupling was repeated once. An
aliquot of the resin was cleaved with TFA-H2O-CH2Cl2 (15:5:80) (0.5 mL, 1
x 20 min). The title compound was purified by semi-preparative reversed
HPLC. Formation of the intermolecular disulfide bridge was obtained
bytreatment of the resin-bound tetrapeptide with I2 (57 mg, 0.225 mmol,
0.06 M) in DMF (2 x 10 min). The resin was repeatedly washed with CH2Cl2
(10 x 1 min), DMF (10 x 1 min), and CH2Cl2 (10 x 1 min). The dimerized
peptide was then cleaved from the resin by treatment with TFA-H2O-CH2Cl2
(3:1:6) (5 mL, 2 x 30 min), and the mixture evaporated with N2, and
lyophilized. The dimer was dissolved in CH2Cl2and added to a solution of
HOAt (10.1 mg, 0.07 mmol) in DMF-CH2Cl2 (1:9), and the mixture was
stirred for 30 min. Further addition of PyBOP (38.7 mg, 0.07 mmol) and
DIEA (45 μL) to adjust to pH 8.0 allowed the cyclization reaction to
start, which was stirred for 6 h. Then, the solvent was evaporated and
the crude bicycle was redissolved in CH2Cl2 (50 mL), and washed with 5%
aqueous NaHCO3 (3 x 50 mL), and sat. NH4Cl (1 x 50 mL), dried (MgSO4),
and evaporated. An aliquot was purified by semipreparative reversed HPLC.
The pNZ-protected bicycle was dissolved in ACN-EtOH-H2O (4:1:1) and
sodium dithionite (12.1 mg, 0.07 mmol) was added and the reaction was
stirred for 2 h to obtain the unprotected bicycle. After evaporation of
the solvent, the 3-hydroxyquinaldic acid (10.5 mg, 0.056 mmol) was
introduced by reaction with EDC-HCl (10.7 mg, 0.056 mmol), and HOSu (6.4
mg, 0.056 mmol), in CH2Cl2 at 25 °C for 2 days. The solvent was
evaporated and the crude product was then purified by analytical HPLC to
obtain oxathiocoraline, yield 1.7 mg, 7%. [linear gradient (50% to 100%)
of CH3CN (0.036% TFA) into H2O (0.045%) over 15 min, with a flow rate of
1.0 mL/min; tR = 7.9 min]. HPLC-ESMS: m/z calcd for C48H56N10O14S4
1124.29; found, 1125.35 [M + H]+. MALDI-TOF: m/z calcd for C48H56N10O14S4
1124.29; found, 1125.99 [M + H]+. HR-MS: m/z calcd for C48H57N10O14S4
1125.2933 [M + H]+, found 1125.2939. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz): δ 11.35 (s,
1H, OH), 8.98 (d, 1H, J = 6.4 Hz, NH Ser), 7.99 (m, 1H, ar. CH), 7.68 (m,
1H, J = 6.9 Hz, ar. CH), 7.62 (s, 1H, ar. CH), 7.54 (m, 2H, ar. CH), 6.54
(d, 1H, J = 7.9 Hz, NH Gly), 5.79 (dd, 1H,J = 5.1, 10.8 Hz, CHα Cys-S),
4.94 (m, 1H, CHα Gly), 4.87 (m, 1H, CHα Ser), 4.64 (m, 2H, CHα Cys(Me)
and CHβ Ser), 4.42 (dd, 1H, J = 5.1 Hz, CHβ Ser), 3.42 (dd, 1H, J = 11.7,
CHα' Gly), 3.28 [dd, 1H, J = 5.1, 11.3, CHβ Cys(Me)], 3.18 (m, 1H, CHβ
Cys-S), 3.02 (s, 3H, NMe Cys-S), 2.96 [m, 1H, CHβ Cys(Me)], 2.85 (m, 2H,
CHβ Cys-S), 2.81 [s, 3H, NMe Cys(Me)], 2.17 (s, 3H, SMe). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 171.8 (C=O), 171.6 (C=O), 171.4 (C=O), 166.7 (C=O), 152.9 (ar.
C), 138.5 (ar. C), 138.1 (ar. C), 130.8 (ar. C), 129.0 (ar. CH), 128.4
(ar. CH), 126.8 (ar. CH), 126.1 (ar. CH), 122.4 (ar. CH), 63.7 (CHβ Ser),
59.0 (CHα Cys), 52.8 (CHα Cys), 51.5 (CHα Ser), 39.9 (CH Gly), 37.1 (CHβ
Cys-S), 33.8 [CHβ Cys(Me)], 31.2 (NMe Cys-S), 29.8, [NMe Cys(Me)], 15.9
(SMe).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction (stages 1-11), 1st stage is attachment to Wang
resin, Alloc removal stage repeated 3 times, subsequent coupling
repeated, stage 10 key step, alternate prepn. described
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid-Phase Synthesis of Oxathiocoraline by a Key Intermolecular
Disulfide Dimer
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tulla-Puche, Judit; Bayo-Puxan, Nuria; Moreno, Juan A.; Francesch, Andres
M.; Cuevas, Carmen; Alvarez, Mercedes; Albericio, Fernando
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2007), 129(17), 5322-5323

