$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: [BocThz-Alloc-oNBS]-TAC scaffold-trityl resin
3: Resin-bound TAC scaffold 2 (0.352 mmol, 1 equiv) was swollen in NMP
(10 mL for 10 min). After ding the solvent the resin was shaken with
piperidine/NMP (1/4, v/v, 3 x 10 mL, each 10 min) and washed with NMP (3
x 10 mL, each 2 min) and DCM (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min). Positive
Bromophenol Blue test indicated Fmoc removal. Next, the Fmoc deprotected
resin was swollen in NMP (10 mL for 2 min). After ding the solvent the
resin was shaken with Boc-Thz-OH (328 mg, 1.41 mmol, 4 equiv), BOP (623
mg, 1.41 mmol, 4 equiv) and DiPEA (490 μL, 2.82 mmol, 8 equiv) in NMP (10
mL) for 90 min and washed with NMP (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min) and DCM (3 x
10 mL, each 2 min). Negative Bromophenol Blue test indicated a complete
coupling of Boc-Thz-OH. [BocThz-Alloc-BocCys(StBu)]-TAC scaffold-trityl
resin 4: For removal of the oNBS-group, resin-bound TAC scaffold 3 (0.352
mmol, 1 equiv) was swollen in DMF (10 mL for 2 min). After ding the
solvent, DMF (10 mL), 2-mercaptoethanol (247 μL, 3.52 mmol, 10 equiv) and
DBU (263 μL, 1.76 mmol, 5 equiv) were added. After shaken the mixture for
30 min, the solution was replaced by an identical fresh solution and
shaken again for 30 min. The resin was washed with DMF (3 x 10 mL, each 2
min) and DCM (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min). Positive Bromophenol Blue test
indicated oNBS removal. After swelling of the resin (2 min) in 10 mL NMP,
it was filtered off and the resin was shaken with Boc-Cys(StBu)-OH (436
mg, 1.41 mmol, 4 equiv), BOP (623 mg, 1.41 mmol, 4 equiv) and DiPEA (490
μL, 2.82 mmol, 8 equiv) in NMP (10 mL) for 90 min, filtered and washed
with NMP (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min) and DCM (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min).
Negative Bromophenol Blue test indicated a complete coupling of
Boc-Cys(StBu)-OH. [BocThz-FmocCys(StBu)-BocCys(StBu)]-TAC scaffold-trityl
resin 5: Resin-bound TAC scaffold 4 (0.352 mmol, 1 equiv) was swollen in
NMP (10 mL for 2 min) and after its removal treated with anilinium
p-toluenesulfinate (1.76 g, 7.04 mmol, 20 equiv) in NMP (10 mL). A gentle
stream of argon was bubbled through the mixture for 10 min and Pd0(Ph3P)4
(122 mg, 0.106 mmol, 0.3 equiv) was added. Argon bubbling was continued
through the reaction for 45 min under the exclusion of light. Next, the
resin was washed with NMP (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min), 0.1% sodium
diethyldithiocarbamate trihydrate in NMP (10 mL for 2 min), 20% DiPEA in
NMP (10 mL for 2 min) and NMP (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min). This entire
procedure repeated once. Then a small aliquot of the resin (ca 5 mg)
microcleavage was treated with 30% HFIP in DCM for 30 min and LC-MS
analysis showed complete removal of the Alloc protecting group. Next, the
Alloc deprotected resin was now swollen in NMP (10 mL for 2 min). Removal
of this NMP was followed by shaken the resin with Fmoc-Cys(StBu)-OH (608
mg, 1.41 mmol, 4 equiv), BOP (623 mg, 1.41 mmol, 4 equiv) and DiPEA (490
μL, 2.82 mmol, 8 equiv) in NMP (10 mL) for 90 min. This was followed by
washing with NMP (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min) and DCM (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min).
A negative Bromophenol Blue test indicated a complete coupling of
Fmoc-Cys(StBu)-OH. [BocThz-Cys-BocCys]-TAC scaffold 6: Resin-bound TAC
scaffold 5 (0.352 mmol, 1 equiv) was swollen in NMP (10 mL for 10 min).
After ding the NMP the resin was shaken with piperidine/NMP (1/4, v/v, 3
x 10 mL, each 10 min) and washed with NMP (3 x 10 mL, each 2 min) and DCM
(3 x 10 mL, each 2 min). A positive Bromophenol Blue test indicated Fmoc
removal. Next, the resin was treated with 30% HFIP in DCM (10 mL for 30
min). The resin was washed with DCM (4 x 10 mL, each 2 min) and the
filtrates were combined and evaporated in vacuo. The crude was then
dissolved in tBuOH/H2O (1/1, v/v) and lyophilized, to yield 349 mg of
crude StBu protected scaffold. Next, this crude scaffold (39 mg, 40 μmol,
1 equiv) was treated with a freshly prepared solution of NaH2PO4・2H2O (30
mM, 94 mg), TCEP (30 mM, 172 mg, 600 μmol, 7.5 equiv per StBu disulfide),
pH 7.5 in 20 mL of H2O/MeCN (1:1) and the mixture was stirred for 3
hours. Next, the mixture was reduced to ca 10 mL by evaporation and then
lyophilized. Finally, crude scaffold 6 was dissolved in H2O/CH3CN/TFA
(75/25/0.1, v/v/v) and purified by preparative HPLC (method A). Fractions
corresponding to the product were pooled and lyophilized to yield
scaffold 6 as a white fluffy solid (22.7 mg, corresponding to a overall
yield of 72%). tR = 27.6 min (method B); HRMS m/z calcd for C35H55N6O9S3
[M + H]+ 799.3187, found 799.3168.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction (except the last stage), attachment to resin
stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Synthesis of Protein Mimics by Sequential Native Chemical
Ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
