$DATUM Protected coupled product 9b: The benzyloxy carbonyl protected amine 6b
(0.222 g, 0.610 mmol) was dissolved in 8 mL of MeOH and 20 mg 10% Pd on
carbon was added and an atmosphere of hydrogen was established with a
balloon. The mixture was stirred at room temperature and pressure for 1 h
and filtered through Celite®. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced
pressure. In a separatory funnel, the dicycohexylamino salt 8 (0.134 g,
0.580 mmol) was suspended in EtOAc and washed two times with 5% KHSO4,
and then with brine. The organic layer was dried with Na2SO4, filtered
and solvent removed under reduced pressure. The acid residue was
dissolved in 4 mL of DMF and added to the amine along with HOAt (0.079 g,
0.580 mmol). The solution was cooled to 0 °C and EDC (0.122 g, 0.640
mmol) was added and the solution stirred at that temperature for 3 h. The
solution was poured over 1 N HCl and extracted 3 times with EtOAc. The
combined organic layers were washed with water, 5% NaHCO3, and brine. The
organic layer was dried with Na2SO4, filtered and the solvent removed
under reduced pressure. The residue was flash chromatographed on silica
gel using gradient elution (100% hexanes to 2 hexanes: 1 EtOAc) to
provide 0.190 g of diastereometrically pure coupled product in 75% yield
determined by 1H NMR. 9b, yield 0.190 g, 75%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CD3OD) δ
7.27- 7.15 (m, 5H,), 4.53 (s, 2H), 4.44-4.37 (m, 2H), 4.21 (q, 2H, J =
7.16 Hz), 4.09 (dd, 1H, J = 3.79, 16.48 Hz), 3.83 (dd, 1H, J = 11.23,
16.53 Hz), 3.24 (dd, 1H, J = 7.57, 13.90 Hz), 2.93 (dd, 1H, J = 7.70,
13.80 Hz), 2.27 (s, 3H), 1.88-1.41 (m, 6H), 1.28 (t, 3H, J = 7.20 Hz);
13C NMR (75 MHz, CD3OD) δ 196.1, 172.7, 172.2, 170.6, 139.0, 130.5,
