$DATUM Method B:
(Benzyloxycarbonyl)-L-valine-L-phenylalanine-piperidine-3R-carboxylic
Acid Ethyl Ester (6b). Compound 5b (21.0 g, 48.0 mmol) was dissolved in
EtOH (500 mL), and 10% Pd/C (1.2 g, 1.13 mmol) was added. The mixture was
hydrogenated overnight and filtered through Celite. The solvent was
evaporated to afford the crude amine (13.2 g). To a solution of the amine
in THF (200 mL) at 0 °C were added Cbz-L-Val-OH (13.4 g, 53.4 mmol), EDC
(10.2 g, 53.4 mmol), and HOBT (7.2 g, 53.4 mmol). The mixture was stirred
overnight at room temperature, and the solvent was evaporated. The
residue was taken up in AcOEt (500 mL) and washed with H2O (2 × 100 mL).
The organic phase was dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated. The residue was
purified by FCC (AcOEt/Hexane 1:1). 6b (21.0 g, 82%) as a colorless oil.
[α]20 D= -31.1 (c =2.0, EtOH); rt = 5.86 min; 1H NMR (DMSO, 120 °C, 400
MHz) δ 0.82 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 6H), 1.18 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.25-1.38 (m,
1H), 1.50-1.65 (m, 2H), 1.81-1.90 (m, 1H), 1.96 (dsept, J = 6.8, 6.6 Hz,
1H), 2.03-2.18 (m, 1H), 2.85 (dd, J = 12.6, 6.3 Hz, 1H), 2.80-2.90 (m,
1H), 2.96 (dd, J = 12.6, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 2.91-3.02 (m, 1H), 3.75-3.85 (m,
1H), 3.89 (dd, J = 9.0, 6.2 Hz, 1H), 3.97-4.05 (m, 1H), 4.07 (q, J = 6.6
Hz, 2H), 5.01 (m, 1H), 5.03 (s, 2H), 6.68 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.12-7.38
(m, 10H), 7.74 (d, J = 6.2 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125.6 MHz, 1:1
mixture of two conformers) δ 14.1, 14.2, 17.5, 19.2, 23.7, 25.0, 26.9,
27.2, 31.2, 31.4, 39.7, 40.3, 40.6, 41.1, 42.4, 43.9, 45.7, 47.3, 49.9,
60.1, 60.2, 60.7, 66.9, 67.0, 127.0, 127.1, 128.0, 128.1, 128.4, 128.5,
128.6, 129.4, 129.7, 135.9, 136.1, 136.3, 156.3, 169.3, 169.5, 170.4,
170.5, 172.3, 172.9; IR (KBr) ν max 3298, 2961, 1730, 1630, 699; HRMS:
Calcd for C30H39N3O6 [M + Na]+ 560.2736, found 560.2745.
