$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Boc-Ala-Gly-Pro-Ile-NHBn 26. Compound 25 (347 mg, 0.8 mmol) was
vigorously stirred with 10% Pd-C (50 mg) in methanol (40 mL) under 4 bars
of hydrogen for 1 hr at room temperature. The catalyst was removed by
filtration, washed with methanol and DCM and the filtrate was evaporated
under reduced pressure. A mixture of the crude product and isoleucine
benzylamide trifluoroacetic salt (132 mg, 0.8 mmol) was treated with DIEA
(418 μL, 3 equiv.), HOBT (123 mg, 0.8 mmol) and DCC (183 mg, 0.88 mmol)
in DCM (20 mL) overnight at room temperature. The reaction was quenched
by addition of several drops of acetic acid and the precipitate was
removed by filtration. The filtrate was evaporated to dryness and the
crude product was purified by silica gel flash chromatography
(chloroform:methanol 95:5) without prior workup. 26. Yield 348 mg, 80%.
1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.33-7.14 (m, 7H), 6.81 (bt, J = 5.4, 1H), 5.32 (bd, J
= 7.6, 1H), 4.52 (bt, 1H), 4.41 (dd, J = 5.9, J' = 11.6, 1H), 4.27 (m,
3H), 3.99 (dAB, δA = 4.07, δA = 4.05, δB = 3.94, δB. = 3.92, JAB = 16.9,
JA'B' = 17.0, 2H), 3.65 (bm, 1H), 3.45 (bm, 1H), 2.25-1.85 (bm, 4H), 1.43
(s, 9H), 1.33 ( d , J = 7.5, 3H), 1.10 (m, 2H), 0.88 (m, 6H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 173.2, 171.5 (minor) + 171.3 (major), 171.0, 168.0, 155.5
(major) + 155.3 (minor), 138.1 (major) + 137.8 (minor), 129.0 (minor) +
128.6 (major), 128.2 (minor) + 127.6 (major), 127.4 (minor) + 127.3
(major), 80.0, 60.4 (major) + 60.1 (minor), 58.1 (major) + 57.7 (minor),
49.8, 49.1, 47.0 (minor) + 46.7 (major), 43.4, 42.1 (major) + 41.7
(minor), 37.4 (minor) + 36.3 (major), 33.9 (major) + 32.1 (minor), 28.5
(minor) + 28.3 (major), 25.6, 24.9 (minor) + 24.7 (major), 19.0 (minor) +
18.6 (major), 15.6 (major) + 15.4 (min), 11.2 (major) + 10.8 (minor).
