$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-(4-Chlorophenyl)-1-{4-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]piperazin-1-yl}-2-(pyridin-3-yl)ethanone
(7). Acid 12 (3.0 g, 12.1 mmol), HATU (4.60 g, 12.1 mmol), and
1-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]piperazine (13) (2.78 g, 12.1 mmol) were
dissolved in N,N-dimethylformamide (30 mL) and treated with
diisopropylethylamine (3.18 mL, 18.2 mmol). The mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 3 h and then partitioned between ethyl acetate and
water. The organic layer was washed with water (×3) and then brine, dried
(MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated under vacuum, and the crude residue
was purified by column chromatography (Flashmaster II ethyl
acetate/hexane/ methanol gradient) to give 7 as an off-white foam (4.2 g,
75%). Preparation of
4-[2-(4-[5-(Trifluoromethyl)pyridin-2-yl]piperazin-1-yl)-2-oxo-1-(pyridin-3-yl)ethyl]benzonitrile
(44).
2-(4-Bromophenyl)-2-(pyridin-3-yl)-1-[4-[5-(trifluoromethyl)pyridin-2-yl]piperazin-1-yl]ethanone
(S60). Acid S56 (1.63 g, 5.58 mmol) was transformed as for the
preparation of compound 7 using aryl piperazine S54 (1.29 g, 5.58 mmol),
HATU (2.10 g, 5.58 mmol), N,N-dimethylformamide (12 mL) and
diisopropylethylamine (1.46 mL, 8.37 mmol) to give bromide S60 as an
off-white foam (2.05 g) contaminated with residual N,N-dimethylformamide
(~15mol% by NMR) and tetramethylurea (~15mol% by NMR). This material was
used without further purification. Bromide S60 (2.00 g, 3.96 mmol ) was
dissolved in N,N-dimethylacetamide (14 mL) and treated with potassium
carbonate (602 mg, 4.35 mmol), potassium hexacyanoferrate(II) trihydrate
(3.5 g, 8.3 mmol) and palladium acetate (177 mg, 0.79 mmol) and the
reaction fitted with a nitrogen balloon and heated to 135 °C. After
stirring at this temperature for 2 hours TLC analysis indicated
consumption of the starting material and the reaction was cooled to room
temperature and diluted with ethyl acetate (150 mL). Undissolved material
was removed by filtration through a pad of celite and the filtrate washed
with water (x5) then brine, dried (MgSO4), filtered and concentrated
under vacuum. The residue was partially purified by Flashmaster II
chromatography (50g column, eluting with hexanes/ethyl acetate gradient
then ethyl acetate/methanol gradient) then further purified by silica
flash column chromatography (eluting with 20% acetone in hexanes
increasing to 33% acetone in hexanes then 100% ethyl acetate) to give the
parent racemate of 44. White foam, yield 680 g, 28% (2 steps). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) 8.56 (br. d, J = 4.3 Hz, 1H), 8.52 (br. s, 1H), 8.39
(br. s, 1H), 7.59 - 7.70 (m, 4H), 7.35 - 7.42 (m, 2H), 7.28 - 7.33 (m,
1H), 6.61 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 5.29 (s, 1H), 3.79 - 3.90 (m, 2H), 3.48 -
3.69 (m, 6H); LCMS [M+H] = 452.4; HPLC (water/ACN + 0.1% TFA gradient)
98.6% at 254nm. Chiral resolution by preparative chiral HPLC using the
following conditions. First eluted enantiomer = E1 (>99.9% e.e.), second
eluted enantiomer = 44 (98.5% e.e.). Instrument: MG preparative SFC;
Column: ChiralCel OD, 250×50mmI.D; Mobile phase: A for CO2 and B for
methanol (0.1% NH3.H2O) ; Gradient: B 25% ; Flow rate: 200mL /min; Back
pressure: 100bar; Column temperature: 38 °C Wavelength: 220nm; Cycletime:
7.2min. The NMR spectral data for the separated enantiomers were
identical with the racemate.
