$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (S)-MTPA amide (11a)A mixture of 9 (12.8 mg,
0.02 mmol) and 10% Pd(OH)2/C (5 mg) in MeOH (3 mL) wasvigorously stirred
under H2 atmosphere at room temperature for 30 min. The catalyst was
filtered off through Celite pad, and the filtrate was concentrated in
vacuo. The residue in CH2Cl2 (300 μL) was treated with (S)-MTPA (4.7 mg,
0.02 mmol), HOBt (8.1 mg, 0.06 mmol), and EDCI (11.7 mg,0.06 mmol) at 0
°C for 5 h. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The residue
was purified by preparative TLC (17% MeOH-CHCl3) to afford 11a (12.6 mg,
89% in 2 steps) as a white foam (R)-MTPA amide (11b)Compound 11b was
prepared from 9 (12.8 mg, 0.02 mmol) and (R)-MTPA (4.7 mg, 0.02 mmol)
asdescribed above for the synthesis of 11a. Purification by preparative
TLC (17% MeOH-CHCl3)afforded 11b (11.0 mg, 78% in 2 steps) as a white
foam: [α]D22 +33.7 (c 0.63, CHCl3); 1H NMR(CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 7.6957 (d,
1H, NH, JNH,6’ = 8.2 Hz), 7.5362 (m, 2H, phenyl), 7.4089-7.2634(m, 8H,
phenyl), 7.1632 (d, 1H, H-6, J6,5 = 8.1 Hz), 5.7901 (d, 1H, H-5, J5,6 =
8.1 Hz), 5.4955 (d,1H, NHCH2OBn, J = 9.8 Hz), 5.4480 (d, 1H, NHCH2OBn, J
= 9.8 Hz), 5.3670 (d, 1H, H-1’, J1’,2’ =2.4 Hz), 5.0688 (dd, 1H, H-2’,
J2’,1’ = 2.4, J2’,3’ = 6.7 Hz), 5.0216 (dd, 1H, H-3’, J3’,2’ = 6.7, J3’4’
=4.2 Hz), 4.7724 (dd, 1H, H-6’, J6’,NH = 8.2, J6’,5’ = 2.8 Hz), 4.6990
(S, 2H, NCH2OCH2Ph), 4.4395(m, 1H, H-5’=, 4.2723 (t, 1H, H-4’, J4’,5’ =
3.2, J4’,3’ = 3.2 Hz), 3.8494 (d, 1H, OH, JOH,5’ = 7.0 Hz),3.7547 (S, 3H,
COCH3), 3.2530 (S, 3H, OCH3), 1.5477 (S, 3H, acetonide), 1.3525 (S, 3H,
acetonide);13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 170.0, 166.3, 162.1, 151.3, 142.3,
137.7, 131.8, 129.5, 128.6, 128.4,128.0, 127.8, 127.6, 115.1, 102.5,
98.3, 87.2, 82.7, 81.3, 72.4, 71.2, 70.3, 55.0, 54.5, 52.8, 27.1,25.2;
FABMS-HR (NBA) calcd for C33H37N3O11F3 708.2380, found 708.2371.
