$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM NovaSyn TGA resin (1.0g, loading 0.28 mmol/g) was swollen with DMF for 30
min in a 3-way glass reactor. DSC (717 mg, 10 equiv) and
N,N-dimethyl-4-aminopyridine (DMAP, 34 mg, 1.0 equiv) in DMF (7 ml) were
added to the resin and the reaction went on for 2 hr at room temperature
with continuous mechanical shaking. The resin was washed with DMF (6×),
followed by addition of a solution of Fmoc-Lys-OAll (1.2 g, 10 equiv),
N,N-diisopropylethyl amine (DIPEA, 0.975 ml, 20 equiv) in DMF (6ml).
After 6 hr of mechanical shaking the reaction was stopped by draining,
then washing with DMF (6×), dichloromethane (DCM, 4×), DMF (4×). The Fmoc
protecting group was cleaved by 20% piperidine/DMF solution (3 × 6 ml ×
10 min). The resin loading can be estimated by determining the
concentration of Fmoc cleavage product in the solution. Using an
extinction coefficient of 7800 at wavelength of 300 nm, through Beer’s
Law, the resin loading was estimated to be 0.17 mmol/g. Linear and cyclic
bisintercalator synthesis. For amino acid couplings, 5 equiv of
Fmoc-protected amino acid (relative to the determined resin loading), 4.9
equiv of N-{(dimethylamino)-1H-1,2,3-
triazolo[4,5-β]-pyridino-1-ylmethylene}-N-methylmethan-aminium
hexafluorophosphate (HATU) and 10 equiv of DIPEA in 6 ml of DMF were
reacted for 50 min at room temperature. The unreacted amino termini were
capped with 5% (v/v) acetic anhydride-5% (v/v) 2,6-lutidine in
N-methylpyrrolidone (NMP, 30 min). A 20% piperidine/DMF solution (3 × 6
ml × 10 min) was used to cleave the Fmoc group. Between every two steps,
the resin was washed with DMF (6×), DCM (4×), and DMF (4×) successively.
For the coupling of Fmoc-Lys(Boc)-NDI monomer to the resin, NDI monomer
(3 equiv), benzotriazol-1-yl-N-oxy-tris(pyrrolidino)phosphonium
hexafluorophosphate (PyBOP, 3 equiv) and HOBt (3 equiv) were dissolved in
NMP (6ml) completely. This solution and N-methylmorpholine (NMM, 6 equiv)
were added to the resin and the coupling reaction was allowed to proceed
for 50 min. After the solvent was drained, the resin was washed with NMP
(6×) and the coupling was repeated. The resin was washed again with NMP
(6×) after the second coupling, followed by the DMF-DCM-DMF washes.
Cleavage of the allyl ester was carried out by treating the resin with
Pd(PPh3)4 (3 equiv) in CHCl3/CH3CO2H/NMM (v/v, 37:2:1) (15 ml /g of
resin) under argon for 2.5 hr at room temperature. The resin was then
washed with 0.5% (v/v) DIPEA/DMF, 0.5% (w/w) sodium
diethyldithiocarbamate / DMF and again 0.5% (v/v) DIPEA/DMF, followed by
the usual DMF-DCM-DMF washes. The final cyclization was initiated by
adding a solution of HOAt (5 equiv), PyBOP (5 equiv) and DIPEA (10 equiv)
in 6 ml of NMP to the resin. After 18 hr, the resin was negative to the
Kaiser ninhydrin test. Final cleavage of the linear or cyclic products
was accomplished by treatment with 95/2.5/2.5 TFA/TIPS/H2O (v/v) at 25 °C
for 1.5 hr. The TFA solution was concentrated to dryness, followed by
addition of 10 ml of H2O. The aqueous solution was washed three times
with diethyl ether and lyophilized overnight. The crude linear or cyclic
bisintercalators were dissolved in 0.1% TFA/H2O and purified by
reverse-phase preparative HPLC (Waters, C18 VYDAC HPLC column, Cat.#
218TP1022) using 0.1% TFA/water (v/v) as solvent A and 0.1% TFA/MeCN
(v/v) as solvent B. In order to get extremely pure compounds, two
chromatographic runs were carried out. For the first run, a gradient of
5% of B to 95% of B over 40 min was applied. For the second run, a
typical gradient was composed of three stages: 5% B to 12% B over 1 min;
12% B to 25% B over 43 min; 25% B to 95% B over 3 min. The product
fractions were combined and lyophilized to yield the linear or cyclic
bisintercalators (~1.5% overall) as white powder. yield 2%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction, capping with acetic
anhydride/2,6-lutidine/N-methylpyrrolidone, Fmoc deprotection with
piperidine/DMF, attachment to PEG-based NovaSyn TGA resin in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Pseudocatenane Structure Formed between DNA and A Cyclic
Bisintercalator
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chu, Yongjun; Hoffman, David W.; Iverson, Brent L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2009), 131(10), 3499-3508

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME434 STEP1
