$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2S,2'S,3aR,3'aR,8aR,8'aR)-1,1'-Bis-((S)-2-amino-3-phenyl-propionyl)-2,3,8,8a,2',3',8',8'a-octahydro-1H,1'H-[3a,3'a]bi[pyrrolo[2,3-b]indolyl]-2,2'-dicarboxylic
Acid Dimethyl Ester (12) N-Cbz-L-Phenylalanine3 11 (84 mg, 0.28 mmol, 3
equiv) was added to a solution of tetraamine 5 (40 mg, 0.09 mmol) in DMF
(1.3 mL). The mixture was cooled down to 0°C and Et3N (45 μL, 0.32 mmol,
3.5 equiv) was added, followed by HATU (107 mg, 0.28 mmol, 3 equiv). The
cooling bath was removed and the mixture was stirred for 14 h at 25°C. 5%
Aqueous LiCl (5 mL) was added, the resulting mixture diluted with H2O (10
mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3x 15 mL). The combined organic layers were
washed with 5% aqueous LiCl (10 mL), dried over Na2SO4 and solvents
removed under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel (95:5 CH2Cl2/ MeOH) to give the coupled
tetra-peptide which was used directly in the next step. To a solution of
3 (76 mg) in a 9:1 mixture of MeOH/H2O (6 mL) was added 10% Pd/C (10 mg)
and the vessel purged several times with H2. The mixture was stirred
under 1 atm of H2 for 4 h and then filtered over a pad of Celite®. After
washing the solids with a 1:1 CH2Cl2/ MeOH mixture (15 mL), the collected
filtrates concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel (90:10 CH2Cl2/MeOH) to give 53 mg (81%
combined yield over the two steps) of the title compound as a foam.
(2S,2'S,3aR,3'aR,8aR,8'aR)-1,1'-Bis-((S)-2-amino-3-phenyl-propionyl)-2,3,8,8a,2',3',8',8'a-octahydro-1H,1'H-[3a,3'a]bi[pyrrolo[2,3-b]indolyl]-2,2'-dicarboxylic
Acid Dimethyl Ester (12), 53 mg (81% combined yield over the two steps)
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.5-7.4 (m, 6H, ArH), 7.2-7.1 (m, 4H, ArH),
7.05 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H, ArH), 6.72 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H, ArH), 6.59 (t, J
= 8.2 Hz, 4H, ArH), 5.33 (br, 2H, NH), 4.89 (s, 2H, H8a/H8a'), 3.55 (d, J
= 8.2 Hz, 2H, CHNH2), 3.37 (dd, J = 10.7, 4.7 Hz, 2H, H2/H2'), 3.06 (s,
6H, 2x CO2CH3), 3.01 (dd, J = 11.6, 4.7 Hz, 2H, H3A/H3A'), 2.83 (t, J =
11.2 Hz, 2H, H3B/H3B'), 2.00 (d, J = 13.3 Hz ,2H, CH2Ph), 1.90 (dd, J
=13.3, 8.2 Hz, 2H, CH2Ph) ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 176.4 (s, 2x
CON), 171.1 (s, CO2CH3), 151.4 (s, 2x), 137.2 (s, 2x), 129.9 (s, 2x),
129.4 (d, 4x), 129.1 (d, 4x), 127.7 (d, 2x), 126.9 (d, 2x), 126.1 (d,
2x), 118.0 (d, 2x), 110.0 (d, 2x), 80.1 (d, C8a/C8a'), 59.4 (s,
C3a/C3a'), 58.5 (q, 2x OCH3), 55.2 (d, 2x), 52.6 (d, 2x), 42.7 (t, 2x
CH2Ph), 34.9 (t, C3/C3') ppm. IR (NaCl) ν 3338 (m, NH), 3025 (w), 2950
(w, C-H), 2851 (w, C-H), 1742 (m, CO), 1634 (s, CO), 1606 (m), 1467 (m),
1313 (m), 1231 (m), 1209 (m), 1172 (m), 845 (m), 754 (s) cm-1. MS (ESI+)
m/z (%) 729 ([M+1]+, 8), 385 (41), 365 (100). HRMS (ESI+) calcd for
C42H45N6O6, 729.3395; found 729.3369. [α]D 24 +430° (c 0.19, MeOH)
