$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 8. General procedure for amide formation and
derivatization of the boronic acid tag. To a round bottom flask was added
the free carboxylic acid (1 mmol, 1 eq), HOBt (0.54 g, 4 mmol, 4 eq),
HBTU (1.51 g, 4 mmol, 4 eq), and the appropriate amine (4 mmol, 4 eq).
DMF was added followed by DIPEA (1.4 ml, 8 mmol, 8 eq) and the reaction
was stirred at room temperature over night. The reaction mixture was
transferred to pp vessel charged with DEAP-PS resin. The resin was
vortexed for 1 hr, then it was washed and the product was cleaved. The
filtrate was concentrated and dried under high vacuum. The residue (0.4
mmol) and the appropriate aryl halide (0.5 mmol) were dissolved in
dioxane (5 ml) and K3PO4 (1 mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4(5 mol%) were added. The
reaction was stirred at 100 °C for 4 h, and then cooled to room
temperature. Addition of saturated aqueous NH4Cl (15 ml) followed by
extraction with EtOAc (3 × 15 ml), drying with MgSO4, filtration, and
removal of solvent under vacuo provided the crude product, which was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel.
3-(4-methoxyphenyl)-N,N-dimethyl-5-(4'-methylbiphenyl-4-yl)-4,5-dihydroisoxazole-4-carboxamide
(13). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.40 (s, 3H), 2.99, (s, 3H), 3.04 (s,
3H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 4.79 (d, J= 8.1 Hz, 1H), 5.77 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H), 6.90
(d, J= 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.25-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.43-7.47 (m, 4H), 7.49-7.63 (m,
5H), 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CDCl3) δ 21.1, 36.4, 37.6, 55.3, 60.3, 87.4,
114.3, 121.3, 126.4, 126.4, 127.5, 127.7, 128.1, 128.8, 129.5, 137.4,
140.3, 141.7, 154.9, 161.1, 168.8. IR (Microscope) 3096, 2987, 2820,
1722, 1658, 1667. HRMS (EI) Calcd. 414.1943, found 414.1952.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling (2nd stage), phase-switch synthesis, purification with
DEAM-PS resin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phase-Switch Synthesis with Boronic Acids as Productive Tags
